<!--
    V2Ray nodes. The v2rayN mark.

    The glyph and its blue are the source artwork, unaltered. Only its seating changed: it sits
    on the same squircle every other home-screen tile uses, because the source SVG's own rounded
    square is a different shape from this grid's, and one tile with the wrong corner radius reads
    as a rendering fault rather than as a brand.

    See HomeApp.imageRes: a tile with artwork gets no coloured background drawn behind it.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="1024"
    android:viewportHeight="1024">
    <!-- v2rayN's own blue, taken from the source file. -->
    <path
        android:pathData="M651.264 51.2c92.16 0 138.24 0 188.416 15.36 54.272 19.456 97.28 62.464 116.736 116.736C972.8 233.472 972.8 280.576 972.8 372.736v278.528c0 92.16 0 138.24-15.36 188.416-19.456 54.272-62.464 97.28-116.736 116.736-51.2 16.384-97.28 16.384-189.44 16.384H372.736c-92.16 0-138.24 0-188.416-15.36-55.296-20.48-97.28-62.464-117.76-117.76C51.2 790.528 51.2 744.448 51.2 651.264V372.736c0-92.16 0-138.24 15.36-188.416 20.48-54.272 62.464-97.28 117.76-116.736C233.472 51.2 279.552 51.2 372.736 51.2h278.528z"
        android:fillColor="#409ED7" />

    <!--
        The stepped V, straight from the SVG's second path. Scaled to 0.75 and shifted so the
        glyph's own bounding box (206.73..819.53 x, 239.27..815.64 y) ends up centred on 512,512
        rather than the artboard being centred, which would have left it sitting low and right.
    -->
